## 1. SOURCE RULES (learned the hard way)

1. **Slide-deck .md files are NOT a number source.** The PDF-to-markdown conversion detaches chart values from their axis labels (example: capex series on Q4 deck slide 12 appears as loose numbers). For any chart or table in a deck, **render the PDF page to PNG (pymupdf) into the scratchpad and read the image**. Use the .md only to locate the slide.
2. **Hard numbers come from filings:** yuho (有価証券報告書) for capex by segment (設備の状況), depreciation, cash flow, segment tables, risk factors, raw materials, customers; tanshin (決算短信) for quarterly P&L and balance sheet; decks for management framing.
3. **Japanese prevails.** The English decks are translations (the JP twin of the Q4 FY03/2026 deck is `3825ea4a...`; the English one sits in the root). Where wording differs, quote the Japanese and flag it.
4. **PDF page vs printed slide number.** MTP deck: PDF page = printed slide + 1. Quote PDF pages, not printed numbers, and say which.
5. **Folder labels are not evidence.** "Competidores" holds Fujimi, Nissan Chemical, Mitsubishi Chemical Group. Do not call any of them a competitor, customer or supplier of Fuso unless that peer's own filings (or Fuso's) say so. Fujimi, for instance, formulates CMP slurry; its only yuho in the folder is the **FY03/2013** one (61st term), which shows it was a Fuso customer then. Check the period of every peer file (see `Company/Competidores/_NOTES.md`).
6. **Conflicts between sources must be shown, not resolved silently.** Known open conflict: FY03/2027 net income guidance is 16,600 (Q4 deck, 15-May-2026) vs 19,200 (Q1 tanshin, 7-Aug-2026, marked "no revision"). The gap of 2,600m equals the after-tax value of the 3,694m subsidy (yuho P104) and the H1 forecast moves by the same amount, so the Aug figure probably includes the subsidy [I]. Still check TDnet / the IR site for a notice between May and August 2026 before calling either number wrong. This also tests the note in Segment Prompt v0.2 section 5 that the Workspace guidance row is "wrong": it may only be newer.
7. **Verify the reader's premises.** "Capex has fallen" must be tested against the yuho series and the Q1 balance sheet (construction in progress 4.2 to 17.3 bn yen and facility payables 5.4 to 14.0 bn yen in Q1 FY03/2027) before explaining it.

